#: includes/class-rr-operations.php:378
msgid "Rewards & Referrals stores points transactions, order links, direct referral relationships and referral codes to operate the store loyalty program. A private account-incarnation token and a retained hashed ownership binding prevent a newly created account from inheriting another account’s reward history when a numeric user ID is reused. These ownership proofs are not sent to external services or included in customer statements, plugin privacy exports or support diagnostics. A staff-only search index copies customer names, usernames and email addresses from WordPress. A referral link can set an HTTP-only, SameSite=Lax br_ref cookie for the configured attribution period; the store owner must obtain any consent required before permitting referral tracking through the rr_referral_tracking_allowed filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-rr-operations.php:378
msgid "Optional reward emails use the site mail service. Delivery records store transaction identifiers and status, not copies of the message or recipient address. Accepted/skipped delivery records are retained for 90 days; failed/uncertain records for 365 days; queued notices expire after 90 days. Customer statements and the WordPress personal-data exporter include reward records. Financial transaction amounts, account identifiers and referral history are retained on erasure requests to protect balances and audit integrity. The store owner must review the applicable retention basis. Uninstall preserves plugin data by default; explicit deletion removes owned records. Any Freemius connection has its own opt-in and privacy notice."
